{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778525654181,"sessionID":"ses_1e79f1bebffeycTL0mqF9yWRLz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bf52c6697269ef1c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"Mesenchymal cell"},"output":"Found 25 matches\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json:\n  Line 2:   \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nfibrochondrocyte progenitor cell \\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nFCP- related synonym - abbreviation - PMID: [31871141](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31871141/)\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nA mesenchymal progenitor cell located in fibrocartilaginous tissues, along the fibrochondrocytic differentiation pathway that co-expresses both fibrochondrocyte markers (COL1A1, COL3A1) and mesenchymal stem cell markers (MCAM/CD146, MYLK) in humans. FCP demonstrates colony-forming capacity and multi-lineage differentiation potential toward osteogenic and adipogenic lineages. This cell serves as a progenitor for mature fibrochondrocytes and other meniscal cell types, with differentiation regulated by TGF-β signaling, focal adhesion, and extracellular matrix-receptor interaction pathways.\\n\\nPMID: [31871141](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31871141/)\\nPMID: [36338137](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36338137/)\\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\n\\nMesenchymal cell\\nProgenitor cell \\n\\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\n\\nPart of some ‘ fibrocartilage’\\nexpresses some 'cell surface glycoprotein MUC18'\\nexpresses some 'myosin light chain kinase, smooth muscle'\\nexpresses some 'collagen alpha-1(